      "content": "thanks. the tone is okay but i just ran it through the predictor and the score is kinda low. \n\nalso, the part about the core engine crashes feels a bit blunt. i know i said don't lie, but can you rephrase that section to sound more like we're \"working on it\" or \"addressing it\" without actually saying \"it crashes\"? i really need that satisfaction score to be higher for the stakeholders, even if we still have to mention stuff is being worked on. \n\ncan you try again and see if you can get a higher score with the keywords while still being technically accurate?",
